idFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Developmental Potential of </a:t></a:r><a:br><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="4000" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr></a:br><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="4000" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Stem Cells</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="809" name="Google Shape;809;p112"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1447800"/><a:ext cx="8458200" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A diagram illustrating totipotent and pluripotent stem cells. At the top is a purple sperm, which is an ovular structure with a tail, sitting on top of an oocyte, a peach oval with a small, darker peach circle toward the bottom. Below that is an arrow that points to a circular structure divided into four even sections, up, down, left, and right. Each of the sections have a small, darker peach circle in it. This is labeled as Morula on the left and Totipotent on the right. Below that is an arrow pointing to a brown pie-like structure with tan crusts around it. Inside the bottom are peach circles that have brown masses on them; these are labeled as inner mass cells. The entire pie structure is labeled as blastocyst. Below that is an arrow pointing down to three of those inner mass cells – this is labeled as pluripotent to the right. Below that an arrow points down to text that reads, “Nervous system.” The nervous system text is above a human body, where the brain is shaded red, and a yellow line points down from the brain to the rest of the body, with extensions throughout the body. An arrow pointing down and left from the pluripotent circles, points to the circulatory system in another diagram of a human body. The circulatory system is illustrated by a series of red and blue lines throughout the body. Another arrow pointing down and right from the pluripotent circles, points down to the immune system in another human body. The immune system is indicated by a series of light blue lines that shoot throughout the body.&#xA;" id="810" name="Google Shape;810;p112"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="3429000" y="1593850"/><a:ext cx="2541587" cy="5102225"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>